    "Budgets close at every tested grid in all four pilot cases; no sediment is discarded or manufactured by the assignment constraint. The prescribed inflow calculation is unchanged within an event. Later flux amounts can change through feedback because the next boundary donor column has changed.",
    "A fixed incoming slot removes alternatives from global matching; retained packets on augmenting paths must use other slots. These changes alter per-column inventories and deposition accommodation, and later transport carries those differences into the model interior.",
    "For coupledA, the newu7@9200 boundary-associated deficit largely disappears, but five original8400 interval regressions return. Conserved total sediment does not imply stable per-column deposition or thickness."
